### DisputeDesk Part 0 — the legacy API, exercised by hand.
### Run with the IntelliJ HTTP client or the VS Code REST Client extension.
### Notice how much the CALLER must already know. That is the problem Part 1 onward solves.

@host = http://localhost:8081

### 1. Who is Priya?
GET {{host}}/api/cardholders/CH-1001

### 2. Her last 30 days. Spot the two identical URBANNEST*ONLINE charges yourself.
GET {{host}}/api/cardholders/CH-1001/transactions?days=30

### 3. S1 — the form makes HER find and supply the other transaction's ID
POST {{host}}/api/disputes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardholderId": "CH-1001",
  "transactionId": "TXN-100103",
  "reasonCode": "DR-101",
  "statement": "I was charged twice for the same order at UrbanNest.",
  "duplicateOfTransactionId": "TXN-100102"
}

### 4. S1 again, as most real cardholders would fill it in — no duplicate ID. -> 422 MISSING_REQUIRED_EVIDENCE
POST {{host}}/api/disputes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardholderId": "CH-1001",
  "transactionId": "TXN-100102",
  "reasonCode": "DR-101",
  "statement": "Charged twice at the furniture shop last week!"
}

### 5. S5 — merchant already refunded. -> 422 ALREADY_REFUNDED
POST {{host}}/api/disputes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardholderId": "CH-1002",
  "transactionId": "TXN-100202",
  "reasonCode": "DR-104",
  "statement": "Order never arrived from QuickCart.",
  "expectedDeliveryDate": "2026-01-01"
}

### 6. S7 — Meera picks "fraud" for a legitimate tea shop with a cryptic descriptor.
###    The form ACCEPTS it and burns a fraud analyst's time. No rule can catch this;
###    only understanding the descriptor can. Remember this one for Part 2.
POST {{host}}/api/disputes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardholderId": "CH-1003",
  "transactionId": "TXN-100301",
  "reasonCode": "DR-201",
  "statement": "I do not recognise SQ *TPR HSPTLTY at all."
}

### 7. Inspect a dispute (replace the ID with one returned above)
GET {{host}}/api/disputes/DSP-10001

### 8. Provisional credit. Send it TWICE and look at provisionalCreditTotal. (Part 4.)
POST {{host}}/api/disputes/DSP-10001/provisional-credits
Content-Type: application/json
X-Actor: analyst:demo

{ "amount": 2000.00 }

### 9. Karan's history — three lost disputes (Part 6 uses this)
GET {{host}}/api/cardholders/CH-1004/disputes
